but it's crazy as shoot week here and so,

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.630
we've been packin' a lot of stuff in.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:17.624
So I did block the time and
made sure I went to bed early.

00:10:17.624 --> 00:10:19.660
And I wanted to be super hydrated.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.410
I knew we had a big shoot day.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.550
And so, I opened up Google Docs.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.290
You looked at all the topics.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.260
- Yeah, I did topics and
I got some idea of titles

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.530
based on where we want this show to go.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.840
- Absolutely, so then I ran with those,

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:36.070
and I started to bullet point
points underneath those.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.470
So I would say for me,

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.264
the outline the video is bullet points

00:10:40.264 --> 00:10:43.000
and I also like to have numbers, you know?

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.330
It brings some organization to it.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.830
We've got five points here

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.080
so people can follow along hopefully.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.430
And not just have just
general flowing information,

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.140
what did I walk away with,
but something concrete.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:57.010
This would definitely be
more relevant for education,

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.310
how to, training, when
you're teaching something,

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.730
when you're helping somebody get a result

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.480
moving from point A to point B to point C.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.790
And then I've also learned though,

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.800
that during this phase
you wanna give yourself

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.940
a little bit of margin
to bullet a few points,

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.650
but then also to do further research.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:18.230
So for me this means verifying
and studying out my ideas.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:19.063
So what we've learned,

00:11:19.063 --> 00:11:21.810
especially with doing 100s
of videos on Think Media,

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.060
is I'm like, okay, if I was gonna

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:25.850
tell somebody how to use the best,

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:28.360
how to setup their camera to shoot video,

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:31.070
I'd probably tell 'em to do X, Y, and Z,

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:32.310
and there's like three points.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:34.310
Then what I like to do is maybe watch

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.900
what are other people teaching on this?

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.640
I'll read a few blogs about it.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.227
I'll actually then say,
"You know, what you wanna do

00:11:40.227 --> 00:11:43.290
"is make sure your frame rate
is set to 60 frames a second."

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.010
And then I like to challenge
myself, "Is that true?"

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.820
And then I like to go to blogs and forums.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.340
I actually really, again,

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.770
you haven't pressed
record on the video yet,

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.840
so you haven't actually, you don't wanna,

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.990
it's very hard to go back
and change the video later.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:59.240
You have to re-shoot it if
you said something wrong.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.460
So I like to verify and study my ideas

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:05.600
as much as possible on paper
staring at the computer.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.780
And then, that way I go, "Oh wow."

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.450
And sometimes I'll catch a
nugget from somebody else's video

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.620
where they'll say, "Yeah, I
tried that and it didn't work."

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.680
Or, "Did you know?"

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.770
And I'll be like, "Oh yeah,
that makes perfect sense."

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.120
And it'll just tweak one of my ideas

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.250
and take it to just kind of another level.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.470
It's giving the content
some time to breathe

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:26.030
and if possible, where this
becomes really powerful

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:28.290
is if you do space this out even more.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.580
I found that once you've
planned for a while,

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.120
prepared for a while,
and then taking a break.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:37.100
Go on a run, go on a jog,
take a break, take a nap,

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.040
like get just out of your normal element.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:40.880
I don't know if people are like me,

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.448
tell me if you're like
this in the comments.

00:12:42.448 --> 00:12:45.140
If you're then, if you're
doin' something else.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.930
You're driving with your
kids and all of a sudden

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.197
an idea pops into your
head and you're like,

00:12:48.197 --> 00:12:50.430
"Wait a minute, I totally
forgot a whole point."

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.520
Have you ever noticed that happen?

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.353
- Yeah.

00:12:52.353 --> 00:12:54.240
- You let your prepared content breathe

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.700
and it actually makes it stronger

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.080
and you haven't even pressed record yet.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.990
- Yeah, it's so critical that
these steps that we're doing

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:01.810
before we even press record,

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:03.910
it makes shoot days so much easier.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.210
I know we found here at Think Media

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.260
that if we aren't planned,

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:10.790
we will miss entire shoot days
because we end up planning

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.950
these types of things.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:14.190
And one of the things I
love that you've taught me

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:18.110
is that once you start making
those lists, like five things,

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.127
you challenge yourself to say,

00:13:19.127 --> 00:13:21.760
"Well are there seven
steps versus five steps?"

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.080
And really thinking
about are you putting out

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.450
the best content and
are you actually sharing

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.850
everything for that person to
get from point A to point B?

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.513
So the next is the final notes.

00:13:32.513 --> 00:13:33.830
What is that like?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.280
- Yeah, so now, think about this.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:38.030
We've gone through, we've
reverse-engineered the big idea.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.770
We've researched before we pressed record.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.720
We kinda know some keyword
research that we've done.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.280
We've planned out the general title.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.640
We've outlined the video.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.287
And now we're looking at it saying, "Okay,

00:13:47.287 --> 00:13:49.970
"what is it missing and what
else would make it stronger?"

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.810
These are things like should
there be any calls-to-action?

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.550
And this is sort of a deeper
concept we teach in some

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.900
of our training programs called

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.000
like Circular Video Viralocity.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.210
If possible, in the middle of the video,

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.980
if you teach a point, do you
teach that somewhere else,

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.450
in another one of your videos?

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.540
You could link to that, and
that's then being able to say,

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:09.017
just like we kind of did in this video,

00:14:09.017 --> 00:14:10.407
"If you wanna learn more about research

00:14:10.407 --> 00:14:12.777
"before you press record,
click or tap the YouTube card,

00:14:12.777 --> 00:14:14.583
"or click the link in
the description below."

00:14:14.583 --> 00:14:17.360
If I have, I had this written in my notes.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:21.080
That's a call-to-action that
happened during the last phase

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.860
of okay, that's a final note.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.660
Where could I weave in
some things like that?

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.270
Are there any props that we need?

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:29.180
We're shooting a batch of
the "Think Media Show" today,

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.950
and so I brought like
seven different shirts

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.296
just so I could go through
the different shirts

00:14:33.296 --> 00:14:37.150
for the shoot, and so, make
sure I have those prepared.

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.190
Are there people that we need?

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.530
Do we need any help with this?

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.450
Or it's like, "Hey man, can you
be there to help me set up?"

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.657
or and even if you're doin'
this solo you're like,

00:14:44.657 --> 00:14:47.810
"Hey honey, can you make sure
the kids aren't in the house."

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:51.990
Like, looking ahead, what
else, is there any final notes

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.550
and getting that all on paper.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:57.940
Again, if you fail to
plan, you plan to fail.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.730
This is that strategic...

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.350
One of our favorite quotes is Sun Tzu,

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:04.027
author of "The Art of War,"
a famous military general.

00:15:04.027 --> 00:15:08.400
"Every battle is won
before it's even fought."

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.530
And I think that's why a lot
of entrepreneurs are losing

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.470
and a lot of people, content
creators, are losing,

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.130
is because they're so frantic right now.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.290
They haven't taken the time to slow down

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.796
and really strategize,

00:15:18.796 --> 00:15:22.364
to slow down and really
think things through,

00:15:22.364 --> 00:15:24.260
and then follow through.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.730
If every battle is won
before it's ever fought,

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.330
that means we're planning on paper.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:32.650
It means that you're
standing over the battlefield

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.027
with the miniature
characters and thinkin',

00:15:36.027 --> 00:15:37.327
"Okay, am I thinkin' all this through?

00:15:37.327 --> 00:15:39.960
"Do we have the gear we
need, the notes we need?"

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.970
And things can happen because this is

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.260
stuff that gets us tripped up.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.307
Once you even think that
this could be notes about,

00:15:45.307 --> 00:15:48.047
"What gear do I need, what outfit?

00:15:48.047 --> 00:15:49.350
"Do I need to charge the batteries?

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:51.906
"Do I need to make sure
that, oh shoot, that's right.

00:15:51.906 --> 00:15:54.486
"My camera is at my sister's house.

00:15:54.486 --> 00:15:55.890
"I'm not even gonna be
able to shoot tomorrow."

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.800
This stuff happens all the time

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:00.680
and we've noticed that it'll
just trip your shoot up.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.730
You're like, "Tomorrow I'm gonna
get like five videos done."

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.760
I don't know, like give
me an amen in the comments

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.880
if you're like, "Completely."

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.440
I thought Saturday morning was gonna be

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.647
this really effective
thing, and then I was like,

00:16:09.647 --> 00:16:11.747
"Oh that's right, I
didn't plug my camera in

00:16:11.747 --> 00:16:13.583
"and I have to wait hours to charge

00:16:13.583 --> 00:16:15.610
"the battery for my camera."

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.920
All those little types of deal.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.500
I know this could kinda
sound overwhelming,

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.620
but it's actually by investing in energy

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:23.640
in scripting your videos, and
planning them ahead of time,

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.456
that it saves you massive
energy in the future.

00:16:26.456 --> 00:16:29.290
- Yeah, are there any
parts of videos that you

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.830
do like to actually
script out word for word?

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:33.960
What are the key elements
in a video that you think

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.420
need to be in it when people
are actually at the phase

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.070
of getting those video scripts done?

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:42.390
- In my opinion, I think
the most important part of,

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.470
so for me, I'm good with an outline

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.120
and just bullet pointing the points.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.320
And that'll keep me on track,

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.930
maybe adding in some call-to-actions,

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.710
any other notes that need to
be added under each point,

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:55.640
or a disclaimer, or a
by-the-way, you know?

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.910
But the hook, the intro,
the first 10 seconds,

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.630
it could be 30 seconds,
it could even be a minute,

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:03.420
I believe should almost potentially

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.030
be scripted word-for-word.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:08.410
Especially if you're
newer to YouTube videos

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:11.670
and to marketing and
grabbing people's attention

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.500
because they will, people will forgive you

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.720
and watch the rest of the video
if you've set it up right.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.460
But if you mess up those first few seconds

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:21.810
and you don't create some curiosity,

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.290
if you don't hook people's attention

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.630
making them wanna watch more.

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:28.400
If you don't actually set the stage

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.800
for what they're about to learn

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.550
and they're not even
interested in learning more.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.350
If you don't maybe say
there's five points coming up,

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:37.500
or have any kind of nuggets,

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.280
you wanna think through
all those types of things.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.780
And that's probably a topic
for a whole nother episode

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:43.500
of the "Think Media Show" some day.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.270
But yeah, I will oftentimes
write a sentence or two or three

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.480
and I'll try to nail
that hook in that intro,

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.530
and then after that, I
kinda relax a little bit,

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.530
and then just try to
hit the bullet points.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.100
But that's some precious time.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.110
And with everybody scrolling
through the different

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:01.610
social media platforms, you
only have a few seconds.

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.670
There's actually the goldfish rule

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.080
that they did a study,
Microsoft did a study,

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.500
that goldfish have an attention
span of eight seconds.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.660
But humans now, because of
social media and phones,

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.960
our attention span is seven seconds.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:17.800
So Heather, you've got the
attention span of a goldfish.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:18.633
- I know, I feel it.

00:18:18.633 --> 00:18:19.466
(laughing)

00:18:19.466 --> 00:18:21.120
- You do, as do I, you know what I mean?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.950
And so, that means that
like, what are you gonna do

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.240
in those first few seconds to get people

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.560
to watch the rest of the video?

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.780
If you could have the most
life-changing information,

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.200
I mean for, in your video,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.010
but if you don't set the stage right,

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.430
people may never get there.

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:37.220
So invest extra energy when
you're writing your outline,

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.610
potentially scripting your hook.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.830
- So good Sean, thank you
for those five points.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.990
And I think one of the things
that I've learned from you

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.470
is that it's okay to mess up.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.280
As you're going through
and making these videos

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:51.420
and you're doing these
scripts that it's okay

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.320
to not always have it perfect, right?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.966
But then there is that point where,

00:18:55.966 --> 00:18:58.200
when you're producing the video,

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.280
that you can bring your personality to it,

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:03.810
but making sure that you're
hitting these key five things

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:05.492
is something that has massively changed

00:19:05.492 --> 00:19:07.960
my brand and what I've been able to do.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.810
So, if you like this type of
content, we are here for you.

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:14.150
We are creating content just like this

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.570
and I wanna know in the comment section

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:16.760
do you script your videos?

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.970
Let us know, and what type
of videos do you wanna see

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.490
here on "The Think Marketing Show?"

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:23.970
Thanks for checkin' out this episode.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.910
We hope you got a ton of value
and if you haven't already,

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.090
subscribe here to "The
Think Marketing Show"

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:31.470
wherever you're watching or listening.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:33.610
- And hey, it would mean the world to us

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:37.410
if you would rate and review
this show on Apple Podcasts.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:39.990
- As we grow this movement
of purpose-driven content

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.800
creators, we encourage you
to share it with a friend.

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.162
And we'll see you in the next episode.

